//RS /// c109 Phase 13: a closure-taking core call (`tasks.spawn`, the legacy
//RS /// address/handler `http.serve`, or `scope.guard`) inside the subset? These
//RS /// are NOT in `core_fixed_sig` — each has a bespoke emit shape. We cover only
//RS /// the cleanest, byte-reproducible case for each, where the closure arg is a
//RS /// LITERAL in-subset lambda:
//RS ///   - `http.serve(addr, <lambda>)` — 2 args; arg0 (addr) any in-subset value, arg1 a
//RS ///     literal lambda (the `jet_http_serve(&(addr), <lambda>)` branch). The
//RS ///     router-handler branch needs an HTTPRouter value, which can only come from
//RS ///     `http.router()` (not in `core_fixed_sig`) — so it can't arise in a covered fn.
//RS ///   - `scope.guard(<lambda>)` — 1 arg, a literal zero-param lambda.
//RS ///   - `tasks.spawn(<lambda>)` — 1 arg, a literal zero-param lambda.
